## Appended by Stage 2a, 2026-09-11

The rows above are the PRE-REGENERATION baseline and are never rewritten: they
are what lets any surviving copy be proven genuine. Byte-identical copies of
all eight are in `data/baseline_frozen/`, verified 8/8 OK at the start of Stage
2a and again at its end.

Stage 2a regenerated the synthetic corpus three times. All three directories
are kept; `data/processed/CORPUS.json` names the one in use.

- `corpus_2026-09-11`: DISCARDED. Median coefficient of variation 0.049 against
  an empirical 0.600. The mixture was placed above the 1e-9 quantile of its
  heaviest-tailed component, which put the median dataset's support at 0.65 of
  its own mean.
- `corpus_2026-09-11b`: DISCARDED. Covered 98.6 to 100 percent of the empirical
  range but centred at 0.071.
- `corpus_2026-09-11c`: **IN USE.** 10,000 datasets plus a 50-dataset probe
  set, 0 failed parents, 0 rejected by the validity filter. Seed 20260911,
  configuration and git commit recorded in its own runmeta.json. Reproducible
  on demand with `cd src && python corpus.py <label>`.

Unlike the files above, these ARE reproducible: the seed, the full generator
configuration, the git commit and the library versions are recorded beside the
data. The checksums below pin the specific bytes produced on this machine.

