## Appended by Stage 2a-2, 2026-09-12: corpus_2026-09-12c

`corpus_2026-09-12c` supersedes `corpus_2026-09-12b` and is the active corpus.
It was regenerated once, at the end of Stage 2a-2, after the empirical arm was
rebuilt from raw values and the configuration retuned against it. Seed 42,
10,000 datasets plus a 50-dataset probe set, 0 failed parents, 0 rejected by the
validity filter, 847 s.

`corpus_2026-09-12b` is NOT deleted. It is the comparison that makes the
four-way table in `reports/HANDOFF_stage-2a2.md` possible: both corpora scored
against both empirical arms, so the movement caused by the new data can be told
apart from the movement caused by the retune.

The corpus was generated from commit `ede8e2b` with a dirty working tree. The
only uncommitted file was `CLAUDE.md`, documentation, and no code or
configuration differed from that commit.

