## Appended by Stage 2a-3, 2026-09-14: corpus_2026-09-14b

`corpus_2026-09-14b` supersedes `corpus_2026-09-13b` and is the active corpus.
10,000 datasets plus a 50-dataset probe set, seed 42, 0 failed parents, 0
rejected by the validity filter, 862 s.

It exists because splitting the empirical arm moved the tuning objective by
1.72 seed-to-seed standard deviations, which is the criterion Stage 2a-3 was
given for reopening generation. Exactly one generation parameter changed:
`cv_log10_sd`, from 0.3752 x 2 to 0.3536 x 2, which is the arm's log10 standard
deviation of the coefficient of variation remeasured on the split arm. Nothing
else was retuned, because no other cited measurement moved.

Match against the 143 empirical datasets, mean standardized W1 across the ten
characteristics 0.252 against `corpus_2026-09-13b`'s 0.262; weighted objective
0.2256 against 0.2352; visible-mode total variation 0.0036. Every
characteristic improved except `w_v_uw_wasserstein`, which moved 0.0015 worse.

`corpus_2026-09-13b` is NOT deleted. It is the comparison that makes the
four-way table in `reports/HANDOFF_stage-2a3.md` possible.

The corpus was generated from commit `25d0937` with a dirty working tree; the
uncommitted changes are the Stage 2a-3 work committed immediately after, and
`src/genconfig.py` differed from that commit by the one field above.

